ashingtonpost.com/lifestyle/2026/06/07/this-couple-grows-trees-shape-chairs-they-sell-90k/</a></p><p>source: <a href="https://marginalrevolution.com/marginalrevolution/2026/06/tuesday-assorted-links-572.html?utm_source=rss&utm_medium=rss&utm_campaign=tuesday-assorted-links-572">Tuesday assorted links</a></p>]]></description><link>https://www.washingtonpost.com/lifestyle/2026/06/07/this-couple-grows-trees-shape-chairs-they-sell-90k/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.washingtonpost.com/lifestyle/2026/06/07/this-couple-grows-trees-shape-chairs-they-sell-90k/</guid><pubDate>Tue, 09 Jun 2026 15:57:55 GMT</pubDate></item><item><title><![CDATA[More comments on phones and fertility]]></title><description><![CDATA[<p><img src="https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/2052934494601048065/6TvQIpAs_200x200.jpg"></p><p>Neeraja Deshpande (@neerajadeshp) on X</p><p>I know this paper aligns with “it’s the phones,” aka the current theory of everything, but the idea that 1/3 to 1/2 of American TFR decline post-2007 was caused by smartphones is absurd. Some concerns: (1) It looks at AT&amp;T expansion from 2008-2011, which precedes the era of</p><p>URL: <a href="https://x.com/neerajadeshp/status/2064017467840586147">https://x.com/neerajadeshp/status/2064017467840586147</a></p><p>source: <a href="https://marginalrevolution.com/marginalrevolution/2026/06/tuesday-assorted-links-572.html?utm_source=rss&utm_medium=rss&utm_campaign=tuesday-assorted-links-572">Tuesday assorted links</a></p>]]></description><link>https://x.com/neerajadeshp/status/2064017467840586147</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://x.com/neerajadeshp/status/2064017467840586147</guid><pubDate>Tue, 09 Jun 2026 15:57:55 GMT</pubDate></item><item><title><![CDATA[Gordon Wood, RIP]]></title><description><![CDATA[<p>URL: <a href="https://www.nytimes.com/2026/06/08/books/gordon-s-wood-dead.html">https://www.nytimes.com/2026/06/08/books/gordon-s-wood-dead.html</a></p><p>source: <a href="https://marginalrevolution.com/marginalrevolution/2026/06/tuesday-assorted-links-572.html?utm_source=rss&utm_medium=rss&utm_campaign=tuesday-assorted-links-572">Tuesday assorted links</a></p>]]></description><link>https://www.nytimes.com/2026/06/08/books/gordon-s-wood-dead.html</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.nytimes.com/2026/06/08/books/gordon-s-wood-dead.html</guid><pubDate>Tue, 09 Jun 2026 15:57:55 GMT</pubDate></item><item><title><![CDATA[It seems Piketty has become a degrowther]]></title><description><![CDATA[<p><img src="https://pbs.twimg.com/media/HJ6gSPpWEAAAdrP.png:large"></p><p>Thomas Piketty (@PikettyWIL) on X</p><p>The key finding of the report is that energy transition alone will not suffice. We need to combine it with “sufficiency” to stay within 2 degrees. This includes labour hour reductions, growth caps in rich countries, less material consumption, and changes in food habits.</p><p>URL: <a href="https://x.com/pikettywil/status/2062413196967784652?s=61">https://x.com/pikettywil/status/2062413196967784652?s=61</a></p><p>source: <a href="https://marginalrevolution.com/marginalrevolution/2026/06/monday-assorted-links-563.html?utm_source=rss&utm_medium=rss&utm_campaign=monday-assorted-links-563">Monday assorted links</a></p>]]></description><link>https://x.com/pikettywil/status/2062413196967784652?s=61</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://x.com/pikettywil/status/2062413196967784652?s=61</guid><pubDate>Mon, 08 Jun 2026 16:43:05 GMT</pubDate></item><item><title><![CDATA[Luis Garicano 🇪🇺🇺🇦 (@lugaricano) on X]]></title><description><![CDATA[<p><img src="https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/1088718721785434112/TCQN0rTD_200x200.jpg"></p><p>Luis Garicano 🇪🇺🇺🇦 (@lugaricano) on X</p><p>This plan is incompatible with freedom- a global class of planners telling us how long to work, how much we can grow, what we can eat. It is also completely wrong. All advances for climate (including the huge drop in battery and solar and wind costs) have come (and will come)</p><p>URL: <a href="https://x